 * `mapping_node`: `/scan` + `map → base_link` → `/map` (latched), `/map_entropy`.
 
+**Status: planned, nothing built (plan written 2026-10-10, while Phase 3 is still open).**
+The two bullets above are the original scope and are unchanged. The planning is in
+`docs/phase-4-mapping/`: [problem](phase-4-mapping/problem.md),
+[implementation](phase-4-mapping/implementation.md),
+[benchmark](phase-4-mapping/benchmark.md). In outline:
+
+* **What kind of claim.** Phase 4 is mapping with known poses, and its claims are *not*
+  rates. "The map is accurate against the analytic ground truth of the world" is judged on a
+  few representative runs, each reported on its own with its spread, and carries no success
+  rate, no Wilson interval and no trial set. The other claims are deterministic (replay gives
+  a bit-identical grid; unit and property tests of the grid) or are a latency distribution
+  over the scans of a run. Reasons, and what is explicitly not claimed, are in
+  `problem.md` section 4. **This split is a proposal awaiting confirmation.**
+* **Pose source, stated rather than hidden.** Until Phase 3 closes, `mapping_node` runs with
+  `pose_source:=ground_truth` (the simulator's `/ground_truth/pose`), a mode that has to be
+  named in the node's diagnostics and in the run's `summary.yaml`. `pose_source:=tf`
+  (`map → base_link` from the real estimator) is the Phase 3 integration and is not built
+  or claimed until Phase 3 is closed. No Phase 4 result may be described as using an
+  estimated pose before then.
+* **Staging.** (1) pure crate: grid, inverse model, ray integration, entropy, accuracy
+  metrics; (2) ESDF on top of the existing exact EDT; (3) node, harness and verdict script
+  on ground-truth pose; (4) reference implementations for cost and agreement; (5) the
+  estimated-pose integration, after Phase 3. TSDF and quadtree (Ch. 19) are last and their
+  place in Phase 4 is an open question, since nothing before Phase 5 consumes them.
+* **Evaluation.** Internal, against the world file's geometry, not against another stack:
+  surface error, completeness, false-occupied and false-free cells, coverage, entropy as a
+  progress trace (never alone), and per-scan update latency as median/95th/99th percentile.
+  Nav2 has no known-pose mapper to compare against (`slam_toolbox` estimates its own pose,
+  `nav2_costmap_2d` is a costmap with different semantics); what is compared, and why, is in
+  `benchmark.md` section 3.
+* **Naming.** Following Phase 3 (`robotics_localization` crate,
+  `robotics_localization_bridge` package), the library is `crates/robotics_mapping` and the
+  nodes will live in `ros2_ws/src/robotics_mapping_bridge`. `ARCHITECTURE.md` still lists
+  the node package as `robotics_mapping`; it is not edited here.
+
+Phase 3 is not closed by this plan: the Nav2/rclpy benchmark and the remaining Phase 3
+items above are untouched and still open.
